course: dictionary
lesson: 11323
title: Yin and yang: opposites that balance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Yin is a word from old Chinese thinking. In that idea, yin and yang are two opposite forces that balance each other in everything, a bit like day and night.
explain: Yin is the dark, cool, quiet, soft side. Yang is the opposite side. Neither one is better; they need each other to make a whole, just as the black and white parts of a circle fit together.
explain: People also use the idea in everyday talk. «They are the yin and yang of the team» means two people are very different from each other, but they fit together well.
explain: When you meet yin in a new sentence, look at the words around it. Is the text about opposites, or about a sound or a shade? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Yin is a noun, and it is usually used in the phrase «yin and yang».
fact: The yin-yang symbol is a circle made of black and white parts.
fact: In Mandarin, «yīn» is a Chinese syllable with several meanings, such as «shady, cloudy» or «sound».
fact: In Scotland, «wee yin» means little one, as in «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin».
fact: «Braw» is Scots for lovely.
exercise: In the old Chinese idea, what is yin? | A loud, bright, busy side | *The dark, cool, quiet, soft side | A town by the sea | A kind of fruit
exercise: In «Ah, they're braw, cheers, wee yin», what does «wee yin» mean? | Big giant | *Little one | Loud noise | Good friend
exercise: What does «braw» mean? | *Lovely | Cold | Rude | Tiny
test: «They are the yin and yang of the team.» What does this mean? | They play in the dark | They always lose | They are the same in every way | *They are opposites that fit together
test: The yin-yang symbol is a circle of what? | Blue stripes only | *Black and white parts | A square of gold | Red and green parts
exam: Which is true about «yīn» in Mandarin? | *It is a Chinese syllable with several meanings | It always means dark and cool only | It is a kind of car | It is a Scottish word meaning one
